---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="Medway Genealogy Research">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Dorset family-history project</div>
    <h1>Tracing the Medway / Meadway line through primary evidence.</h1>
    <p class="lead">This site records the evidence, hypotheses, contradictions and next archival steps in the reconstruction of the Medway family from Hamworthy and Poole back into eighteenth-century Lytchett Minster, Purbeck and earlier Dorset lines.</p>
  </section>

  <h2>Current research focus</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card">
      <span class="status strong">Strong leading hypothesis</span>
      <h3>Mary Galley of Lytchett Minster</h3>
      <p>The leading candidate for Matthew Medway's wife is Mary Galley, baptised at Lytchett Minster on 20 April 1760, daughter of William Galley. The case is strengthened by a Galley network already spanning Lytchett and Hamworthy before her birth.</p>
      <p><a href={`${base}research/mary-galley/`}>Review the evidence →</a></p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="status proved">Proved direct line</span>
      <h3>James Medway, 1800</h3>
      <p>James, son of Matthew and Mary Medway, was baptised at Poole St James on 19 August 1800 and anchors the proved direct line forward through Hamworthy.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="status open">Open question</span>
      <h3>Matthew's origins</h3>
      <p>Matthew Medway, a sojourner at his 1786 Poole marriage, is still being tested against the West Lulworth baptism of 1758 and the wider Purbeck Meadway network.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <h2>Method</h2>
  <p>Every conclusion is separated into proved fact, strong inference and open hypothesis. Original registers, wills, militia lists, court papers, leases and probate documents take priority over derivative indexes or user-created family-tree links.</p>
</BaseLayout>
